  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 335 AM EDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nSouthwest winds will continue to advect moisture into the region \nSaturday, helping boost instability by Saturday afternoon. A weak \nwave translating eastward across TN into the Carolinas may provide \nenough lift for scattered thunderstorms Saturday afternoon into\nSaturday night, especially across north/northeast GA where a \nmarginal risk for severe thunderstorms is in place. The main risk \nwith these storms will be isolated damaging wind gusts.\n\nThe remainder of the long term period will feature lower storm \nchances and increasing temperatures as upper ridging amplifies \nacross the eastern US into the early to middle portion of next week. \nHigh temperatures will climb into the mid to upper 90s for much of \nthe area outside elevated portions of northeast GA, with high \nhumidity values pushing heat indices to near or over 105 degrees \nin some areas.",
